.TH GENESYS-SHELL 1 "2026-08-20" "GenESyS" "GenESyS Manual"
.SH NAME
genesys-shell \- GenESyS command-line shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B genesys-shell
.RI [ application-arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B genesys-shell
is the stable public entry point for the GenESyS command-line shell. It is a
small wrapper that execs
.BR /usr/libexec/genesys/genesys-dispatch (8)
with
.BR "--app genesys-shell" .
The dispatcher selects either the validated per-user runtime referenced by
.I ~/.local/share/genesys/current
or the Debian-provided system fallback installed at
.I /usr/libexec/genesys/system/bin/genesys-shell
and then replaces itself with the selected shell executable. All arguments
given to
.B genesys-shell
are forwarded unchanged to the selected executable.
.PP
.B genesys-shell
never performs a network update check. Update behavior is exclusive to
.BR genesys-gui (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/genesys/update.conf
System-wide administrative runtime-selection policy (conffile).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/genesys/current
Symbolic link selecting the active per-user runtime, if any.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the selected shell executable, or 127 if no valid runtime
could be selected.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR genesys-gui (1),
.BR genesys-worker (1)
